WEBVTT

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.730
I've returned.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:10.610
Were you successful?

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.950
The clown has determined the 
identity of the bishop.

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:17.230
The bishop intends on allying with

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:19.340
the Seven Stars in the 
City of the Singing Princess.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.500
Then, Shadow, you know what needs to be done.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.090
Death to the traitor!

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:30.040
Praise the glory of God!

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.380
Show them our justice!

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:37.350
People, we now begin our celebration.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.240
The apostates will be punished by God.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.320
For the Holy Land of Alsok!

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.370
For the Holy Land of Alsok!

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:19.410
<b>The Cardinal's Celebration</b>

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:25.290
On a scale of zero to a hundred, 
how much do you love me?

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.600
That's an embarrassing question to answer.

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:30.790
Just tell me.

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:32.290
Oh, all right.

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:42.160
Gotcha.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:43.050
What?

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.660
It's a little game to show me
 how great your love is.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.660
If your hand were closer to zero...

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:52.170
Say what? That's stupid.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:53.940
And your laugh is creepy.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:56.890
Hey!

00:02:56.890 --> 00:02:58.300
What?

00:02:58.300 --> 00:02:59.030
Jiv...

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:04.030
I love you, too, Jiv.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:06.400
Hey!

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.790
Aren't we going to the festival today?

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:12.750
I can't hold in my passion.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:16.300
Let's go somewhere else before the festival.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.260
We can't...

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.140
Jeez.

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:32.900
Hello?

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.410
What? Who is it?

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:42.680
Why don't you find
out for yourself, Mr. Soleil?

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.030
You're late.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:55.960
Shut up.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:02.300
Just how many women do 
you have in town, Gigina?

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.550
I don't know.

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:06.050
They just flock to me.

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.740
You womanizer!

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:09.430
You're going to get stabbed one day.

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:10.890
In fact, you deserve to be.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:12.540
No, wait...

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:16.560
How do you even have Jiv's phone number?

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:21.140
We happened to meet at the library, 
and she gave me her name.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:24.570
Since I knew her name, I looked 
her up in the phone book.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:26.660
Are you sure?

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.500
That woman is terrifying.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:34.310
She had the nerve to lecture 
me, a Draken warrior.

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:41.130
"Please don't give Gayus any trouble. 
I won't ever forgive you if you do."

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:44.170
She was unusually intense.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.680
Is she a master of some form of martial arts?

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:50.760
No, she's an ordinary 
half-Alurian office worker.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.620
How suspicious.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:05:00.240
So, your brain's so light it could fly into 
the air, and you were at the library?

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:01.610
What for?

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.530
I borrowed a book.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:05.530
Huh?

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:09.770
A book called <i>One Hundred 
Ways to Train an Animal</i>.

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:12.040
Dunno.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:14.440
The PR people must have 
put it up on their own.

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:17.240
How unfortunate.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:19.970
That aside, you two have a guest.

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:23.760
A top-ranking Jushiki officer
 from headquarters.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.060
Be sure not to offend him.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:28.180
Long time no see, Gayus.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.740
Come on, now. It's me.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:35.020
Have you forgotten the face of your 
toxic friend from your school days?

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:37.440
Helodel!

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.440
You've changed so much.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:43.480
To think the Helodel I knew would be 
a top-ranking officer at headquarters.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:45.900
I assumed you'd be in the military.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:48.780
Ah, sorry.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:53.290
I was in the military for a while, 
but I did some thinking, and...

00:05:54.950 --> 00:06:00.140
So, what does a bureaucrat 
from headquarters want from us,

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:02.090
all the way out here in Eridana?

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:04.150
Ah, sorry about that.

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.840
I can't reveal their name here,

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:12.020
but a prominent figure is 
visiting Eridana at the moment.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:17.100
I'd like to ask you two to serve as 
guides and bodyguards today and tomorrow,

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.960
while said person is here.

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:25.980
Hello, thank you for coming.

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:31.450
By prominent figure, you meant 
His Eminence Cardinal Mouldeen?

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:34.870
There's no need for the 
stuffy greeting, Gayus.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:38.360
I have no fondness for the meaningless.

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:40.960
Let's just be rational 
and get down to business.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:47.180
I understand using locals as guides.

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:52.470
But why did you need to request Offensive 
Jushikiists from the outside?

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:56.220
I thought you have the unrivaled 
Offensive Jushikiists,

00:06:56.770 --> 00:07:00.600
the Twelve Winged Generals, 
under your command.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:04.940
You should have no use for us.

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:09.240
I can't have them come with me.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:12.490
They would ruin my fun.

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:19.440
I order you two to be my tour guides.

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:21.580
Now, let's head to the festival.

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:24.210
Tour? Festival?

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:26.210
That means...

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:28.630
I'm sorry, Jiv.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:35.600
The Eridana Festival celebrates the 
victories of the singing princess Eridana,

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:40.920
who brought the people of this town 
together and guided them to victory

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:43.350
back when it was occupied by foreigners.

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:46.160
Since then, this town has 
been known as Eridana,

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:50.180
City of the Singing Princess, 
and that brings us to the present.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:56.160
Was my request on too short a notice?

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.330
No, not at all.

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:05.630
You really seem to be enjoying the tour.

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:09.120
Have you forgotten that you're a person

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:12.500
of great importance to the 
Dragon Empire, Your Eminence?

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:14.900
That may not be the case.

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:21.310
<i>There's nothing to be gained, 
either for us or for Lapetodes,</i>

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:27.310
<i>in fighting against them for 
control over the Holy Land of Alsok.</i>

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:32.430
That's Genon, one of the 
Twelve Winged Generals.

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:34.570
He's a master of disguise,

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:37.480
able to take on the appearance 
and mannerisms of anyone.

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:40.080
So he's a double?

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:44.720
Yes. All told, there are seven 
Mouldeens throughout the empire,

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:48.460
including Genon and myself.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:52.520
Their sacrifices have saved 
my life quite a few times.

00:08:53.110 --> 00:08:55.660
The more insurance the better, after all.

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.610
It's a bit of a game.

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:00.520
A game?

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:05.690
Is that Jushiki, too?

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:06.760
Yes.

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:11.360
A first-order chemical manipulation 
Jushiki called Lorei.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:13.800
It's practically magic.

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:17.360
It's just technology, 
bound by the laws of physics.

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:20.620
You're quite the pessimist, aren't you?

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:23.620
I'm just pessimistically optimistic.

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:26.120
I see.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:29.260
So long as there are children
who can smile innocently

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.330
as they happily eat sweets,
I have a positive opinion of this world.

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:41.100
To that end, I have deceived, 
betrayed, and spilled blood.

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:43.930
And I'll likely continue to do so.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:47.480
If that isn't enough, 
I'll resort to higher reason.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:51.060
And if that isn't enough, 
higher reason still.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:53.940
Why don't we have lunch?

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:55.640
Now...

00:09:57.890 --> 00:10:00.800
I know, let's have Urk cuisine.

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:02.600
It's my favorite.

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:07.250
Your Eminence! We can't have you making 
sudden changes to your itinerary.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:09.820
What are you waiting for? Let's go.

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:17.920
Say no to the Lapetodes City Alliance's 
ratification of the Tienlun Accord!

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:20.260
Say no!

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:23.760
It's quite unpopular, isn't it?

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:27.560
The Tienlun Accord is an agreement 
between dragonkind's moderates,

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:31.040
the Vaisen, and the human nations.

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:34.860
It exists to avoid unnecessary 
conflict between the two.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:37.900
Yes. The accord, in fact, legally allows

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:42.250
hardline dragonkind to be eliminated 
should they encroach on our territory

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:44.120
past the buffer zone.

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:49.240
Speaking of which, it was you two 
who defeated the black dragon

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:51.460
that entered the buffer zone, was it not?

00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:52.490
Yes.

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:55.840
It comes with some sacrifices, 
but it's certain that the accord

00:10:56.600 --> 00:11:00.730
is what's staving off all-out war 
between humanity and dragons.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:04.100
Do you think they're foolish?

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:05.970
Well...

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:13.110
If you're one of the people who's lost 
your family and loved ones to the dragons,

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:16.860
the accord must come across 
as an unforgivable compromise.

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:22.620
Even so, it's irrational to try to move 
society based on an individual perspective.

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:26.260
Your Eminence...

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:28.250
Let's walk.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:29.870
It'll be faster.

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:37.690
Come on, you slaves of authority,

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:40.760
give me something that'll 
look better on the newspaper!

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:45.760
Helodel, is the security at the hotel ready?

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:47.230
It's all set.

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:48.410
Not to worry.

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:53.480
Then once we arrive there, 
I'll have you leave until the morning.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:55.660
But Your Eminence...

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:58.490
I'm here as a tourist.

00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:01.610
Let's enjoy ourselves tonight.

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:02.400
But...

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:05.340
This is an order.

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:09.640
I'm a great superior, am I not?

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:28.010
Say, where's Gigina?

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.200
Did I make him uncomfortable?

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:32.960
Don't talk to me about him.

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:34.580
You're going to ruin my drink.

00:12:35.220 --> 00:12:39.070
He's probably at the furniture shop 
that he spotted earlier in the day.

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:45.280
Gigina is a 13th grade Offensive Jushikiist,

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:47.380
an Enlightened, is he not?

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:49.410
He must be a dependable partner.

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:54.830
He's a sword dancer who prefers power 
types even against biological types.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:57.210
Even his brain is made of muscle.

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:59.520
I'm a chemical manipulation type.

00:12:59.520 --> 00:13:01.270
We're oil and water.

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:05.750
Still, it's amazing that 
you're working together.

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:10.100
You're already a 12th grade at 
your young age, too, aren't you?

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:14.020
Yeah. I was fortunate enough 
to have a great master.

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:16.310
And I don't mean Gigina.

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:18.310
I know.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:22.150
Oh, by the way, do you remember that Jushiki?

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:23.930
How could I forget?

00:13:23.930 --> 00:13:27.580
It's one of the most infamous pranks 
we pulled when we were in school.

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:31.220
I bet you could pull it off now.

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:33.240
Nope.

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:37.540
It's against the law, and it's dangerous.

00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:40.310
So you've tried it, haven't you?

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:43.850
Enough about that.

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:46.170
You've really made it up the 
ladder, too, haven't you?

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:47.640
A headquarters bureaucrat.

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:50.500
His Eminence Mouldeen's secretary, no less.

00:13:51.780 --> 00:13:53.620
I'm just a babysitter.

00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:57.060
Honestly, I'm a little surprised.

00:14:00.370 --> 00:14:02.190
About Shifaka?

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:04.100
Yeah.

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:12.170
Have you gotten over it yet?

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:15.340
I used to think that being in the military

00:14:15.340 --> 00:14:18.650
and avenging her was the right thing to do.

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:22.460
But I'm different now.

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:25.940
Revenge won't save anyone.

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:28.730
That man is truly great.

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:34.140
I believe in the path of coexistence 
that His Eminence strives for.

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:40.650
What about you? Have you gotten over 
what happened to your sister, Aleciel?

00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:45.800
We shouldn't have asked 
each other about this.

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:58.270
You're finally here.

00:14:58.270 --> 00:15:02.210
Well? Has the messenger arrived 
from the Seven Stars?

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:04.960
Everything is going according to plan.

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:06.380
Excellent.

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:11.130
What about the traitors who stole our things?

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:15.950
They seem to be wandering 
in search of a sacrifice.

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:20.060
They've caused some incidents because 
they aren't in their homeland,

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:21.960
but I've sent a signal.

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:24.310
They'll find a target soon enough.

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:28.160
The performance will be a success.

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:31.000
God and that man will guide us.

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:34.620
Then we must do our part.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:35.400
Yes.

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:42.240
Nonsteroidal anti-inflammatories

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:47.500
and acetaminophen are the two antipyretics.

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:50.840
The latter has fewer side effects.

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:53.480
Helodel?

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:55.360
Are you taking a piss?

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:57.580
You ought not be drunk on the job.

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:03.260
"One cannot swing their 
blade with a tipped glass."

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:06.730
Have you forgotten the Draken 
people's precious teachings?

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:08.540
Be gone, demon!

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:10.360
Pew, pew, pew!

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:12.220
Poisoning psychokinesis!

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:14.520
Don't you dare break without my permission.

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:15.940
We're leaving.

00:16:19.730 --> 00:16:23.580
Long time long see no see, Gigina.

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:27.060
Thank you.

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:34.550
Sir, I can say as a connoisseur that 
the tables in this establishment are splendid.

00:16:35.030 --> 00:16:39.050
The chairs also have a gentle character, 
as well as bewitching legs.

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:41.690
Take good care of them.

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:43.300
Yeah, sure.

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:46.330
But overworking them isn't good.

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:50.570
Each one must have her time off from 
her services and given an opportunity

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:53.160
to see the mountains and beaches.

00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:55.070
Right...

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:58.070
Gigina, you dummy!

00:16:58.070 --> 00:17:00.490
You military freak!

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:03.200
You always spend more money than we earn!

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:05.610
We're barely getting by, you know that?

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:06.830
What am I, a housewife?

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:13.290
I could have been living a simpler 
life if you hadn't picked me up.

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:17.610
I'd be an assistant or researcher 
or something at the academy,

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:20.800
with a cute wife and kids.

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:25.940
The academic path was already closed 
to you when you met me, was it not?

00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:29.820
You also aren't much of a family man.

00:17:31.810 --> 00:17:33.360
Was it?

00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:34.650
Let's continue.

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:40.490
You and I are partners. We inherited 
Diorg's will and office together.

00:17:40.980 --> 00:17:43.660
This is a good time to come clean.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:45.300
If you have a problem with me, say it.

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:50.380
Gigina, you bought more ridiculously
expensive furniture again, didn't you?

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:54.280
The book that I got from the library,

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:56.680
<i>One Hundred Ways to Train an Animal</i>,

00:17:57.330 --> 00:18:01.760
said that it's good to talk to 
an animal once in a while.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:05.520
Believe it or not, I'm doing this 
for the sake for your mental health.

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:09.210
I hate you.

00:18:09.670 --> 00:18:11.260
We'll get along swimmingly, then.

00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:13.850
I absolutely loathe you as well.

00:18:19.840 --> 00:18:22.160
Have I made another mistake?

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:26.370
You humans are hard to tell apart.

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:37.560
Are you the ones who killed my beloved?

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:40.010
You can't be...!

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:42.010
I've finally found you!

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:46.780
Gigina, she's the rumored...

00:18:46.780 --> 00:18:48.220
Jushikiist killer.

00:18:48.220 --> 00:18:50.960
And to think that it was us she was after...

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:52.540
I like it!

00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:08.780
She's a gravity Jushikiist.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:13.620
This blade, the wavelength of this curse...

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:19.510
There's no doubt that
you're my beloved's killers.

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:24.010
I am Nidvork of Urz.

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:32.150
I came here to avenge 
my beloved, Eningiluud.

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:38.530
I don't know who the hell 
you're talking about!

00:19:39.940 --> 00:19:45.160
"Who the hell"? You killed him 
without even knowing who he was?!

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:15.310
Fifth-order gravity Jushiki,

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:16.870
Behemo.

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:20.110
Gravity passes through all kinds of barriers.

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:22.780
There are no effective 
ways to defend against it.

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:23.740
Then...

00:20:40.100 --> 00:20:44.440
Third-order chemical manipulation 
Jushiki, Forkalor.

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:46.200
I may not be able
 to cut your skin with a blade,

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:47.720
but you won't withstand strong acid!

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:50.060
How dare you...

00:20:50.440 --> 00:20:53.060
How dare you use such a curse?!

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:55.430
How much...

00:20:58.350 --> 00:20:59.820
must you insult me?!

00:21:21.620 --> 00:21:24.860
That woman... She called 
herself Nidvork or something.

00:21:24.860 --> 00:21:26.480
Who the hell is she?

00:21:26.480 --> 00:21:27.610
And who is she avenging?

00:21:27.610 --> 00:21:29.080
I don't know.

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:31.880
We have plenty of reasons to be despised.

00:21:31.880 --> 00:21:34.040
I know, but...

00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:39.000
What's that?

00:21:42.640 --> 00:21:44.370
Please stay back.

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:05.960
I'll have their heads someday.

00:22:06.530 --> 00:22:11.400
For now, I'll at least come to you.

00:23:50.760 --> 00:23:53.780
There are two truths that are absolute.

00:23:54.450 --> 00:23:57.780
One is that all people someday die.

00:23:58.450 --> 00:24:04.140
The other is that all 
truths have exceptions.

00:24:02.540 --> 00:24:05.040
<b>Weaver of Light</b>
